 "intro": [
  "Sir Orrin Wren rode to Saint Orrin's Rest to hold it against the Concord, and the Concord sent his own great-grandson. Aldous Wren cut him down at the chapel door and carried the body back to Greyhold to burn it at dawn.",
  "The Regent does not let go of what is hers. Cross the dike, break into Greyhold and bring Orrin's body out of the chapel before the pyre is lit. You have until dawn: twenty minutes. Silencing the chapel bell buys you more.",
  "Aldous himself has ridden north. His town has not."
 ],
 "outro": [
  {
   "text": [
    "Greyhold burns, but not Orrin. Ysmay finds him laid out in the chapel under a Concord banner, and raises him a second time before the walls have stopped smoking.",
    "He opens his eyes and asks only one thing: whether the boy lived. He did."
   ]
  }
